# NOTICE — robyn-aethonan example

This directory is part of the Aethonan project (Fidus Writer fork of Granian) and demonstrates
embedding Aethonan as a Rust library. It contains a vendored and ported copy of the Robyn
Python web framework.

## Robyn

- Upstream: https://github.com/sparckles/Robyn
- Vendored from commit `1170748e` (version 0.88.0)
- Copyright (c) 2021 Sanskar Jethi and the sparckles project
- License: BSD 2-Clause (see `LICENSE`)

The Rust core (`src/`) was ported from actix-web to the Aethonan rlib, and the Python package
(`robyn/`) was minimally adapted to be served by Aethonan's own server classes. Every ported
source file carries a vendored-from header.

## Granian / Aethonan derived code

The files `src/asyncio.rs`, `src/callbacks.rs` and `src/conversion.rs` (and the design of the
executor glue) are adapted from Granian (https://github.com/emmett-framework/granian):

- Copyright (c) 2021 Giovanni Barillari
- License: BSD 3-Clause

Those file-level attribution headers are preserved verbatim.

## Aethonan

Aethonan (https://github.com/fiduswriter/aethonan) is the Fidus Writer fork of Granian and is
BSD 3-Clause licensed. This example embeds it as a library dependency
(`aethonan = { path = "../..", package = "aethonan", default-features = false }`).

## The integration tests

`integration_tests/` is a vendored copy of Robyn's own integration test suite (same upstream
commit, same BSD 2-Clause copyright and license as Robyn above). The test sources themselves
are unmodified; they run against the ported server.

THIS EXAMPLE IS A DEMONSTRATION FORK-PORT. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
Robyn/sparckles project, and it is not a supported Robyn distribution.

## Patched dependency

`patches/pyo3-async-runtimes` is a vendored copy of the
[pyo3-async-runtimes](https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3-async-runtimes) crate
version 0.30.0 (© Andrew J. Westlake, David Hewitt and contributors;
MIT OR Apache-2.0), carrying a minimal fix (marked `AETHONAN PORT PATCH`) for
drops of Python heap pointers on unattached runtime threads, required when
pyo3 0.30 is built with `--cfg pyo3_disable_reference_pool` (the Aethonan
repository's build configuration, which crates inside the repository
inherit). The fix is applied through `[patch.crates-io]` in `Cargo.toml`.
